      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I'm unable to edit the post, but when I made this, I was supposed to state that these were things that I noticed with the Vive Controllers. For some weird reason, the controllers simulated Oculus controllers. The only capacitive part of the Vive wand would be the trackpad. The purpose of this post was to give suggestions to possibly remedy these issues for Vive Wands and potentially port over the features from the current set up we Vive controller users have over to other controller types, as there could be possible controllers like the Reverb G2's controllers that lack capacitive touch, or the Etee controllers which only have a trackpad. Overall would be best to think of this post as more of a consideration for future controllers",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
